\documentclass[11pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=2.5cm]{geometry}
\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}

\title{Pricing Notes for a Pure Endowment Block}
\author{Product and Valuation Team}
\date{July 2026}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section*{Setting}

The block covers lives aged~40 at issue, with benefits payable
only on survival to the end of each term layer. Throughout these
notes the five-year layer is priced off the discount--survival
factor $v^{5}\,{}_{5}p_{40}$.

\section*{Layer Quotes}

For the ten-year layer the same building block is
$v^{10}\,{}_{10}p_{40}$, and the reinsurers quote it separately
from the shorter terms. The fifteen-year tranche appears in the
treaty slip as $v^{15}\,{}_{15}p_{40}$, while the internal
capital model writes the twenty-year leg as
$v^{20}\,{}_{20}p_{40}$.

\section*{Sensitivity Shelf}

A legacy sensitivity run for lives aged~35 keeps the old
notation on purpose: the seven-year factor
$v^{7}\,{}_{7}p_{35}$ is still cited verbatim by the retiracy
treaty, so it is left exactly as written.

\end{document}

\documentclass[11pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=2.5cm]{geometry}
